# Core product

- Single-owner Project Management System. Modular Next.js monolith — no new microservice or framework swap.
- Stack: Next.js App Router, Route Handlers, pg repositories, PostgreSQL 16, Docker Compose.
- Eight menus: `/` Dashboard, `/projects`, `/work-items`, `/board`, `/analysis`, `/daily-work`, `/company`, `/settings`. Do not treat `/tasks` or `/issues` as a second source of truth.
- Thai-first UI, docs, and chat. Keep English system terms (WorkItem, TimeEntry, Company, Project).
- System default time zone in every environment, including application and database sessions, is `Asia/Bangkok`. Persist every date and timestamp using Bangkok calendar/wall-clock semantics; do not convert stored values to UTC.
- Documentation index: `document/README.md`. EV source of truth: `document/requirements/business-requirement.md`, `document/requirements/scope.md`, `document/architecture/engineering-spec.md`, `document/architecture/overview.md`, `document/api/overview.md`, `document/database/overview.md`, `document/database/mapping.md`, `document/operations/deployment.md`. Feature `document/requirements/features/*` marked "done" is UI-only; data/API must follow EV.
- One shared `WorkItem` and `TimeEntry` set. Dashboard, Board, and Analysis are read projections — never mock KPIs in production UI.
- Developer / Infra / SA live only on `WorkItem.role`. They are not accounts, `User.role`, or permissions.
- Multiple Company profiles may be managed per installation, and each Project belongs to one Company. There is one owner `User`; `ProjectMember` is legacy schema, not a product feature.
- Implement in order: (1) server validation + owner access (2) Dhas Company + Project backfill (3) Board + Daily Work consistency (4) Dashboard aggregates (5) Analysis/export (6) Settings persist (7) GitLab import.
